WEBVTT


00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.960
remember anything so fast that it's unbelievable

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.362
You learn three languages, 

00:00:03.362 --> 00:00:04.520
your friends learn 40 minutes.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.269
The next day, 

00:00:05.269 --> 00:00:06.180
he remembers everything. 

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.200
You remember almost nothing.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.880
It's not a talent gap.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.160
It's the technical distance.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.800
And this technique takes five minutes to learn three steps.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.280
The first step sounds like a waste of time.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.560
The last step is why you've forgotten everything.

00:00:16.561 --> 00:00:17.361
right now

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.335
Before you go ahead, 

00:00:18.335 --> 00:00:19.640
leave a comment and let me know.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.280
How do you usually memorize?

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.040
Read and re-read or write on paper.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.760
Comment below so I know and we can fix it.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:26.631
Step one, 

00:00:26.631 --> 00:00:28.960
read it as if you're going to be tested in 10 minutes.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.200
Imagine that AI is telling you that

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.720
There will be a test in 10 minutes.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.040
about what you're about to read.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.000
Every detail is important.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.400
That's the mindset you need every time you sit down to study.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.280
Most people read once and then move on.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:41.640
Read it five times and forget it.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.480
It's not how many times you read it.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:45.200
It's what you do every time you read it.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.320
Think about how you memorize the lyrics.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:49.560
You don't sit back and read you.

00:00:49.561 --> 00:00:51.721
Sing a few words and try again.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:52.720
for the third time.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:53.800
words self-flush

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.925
That's because your brain isn't just scanning, 

00:00:55.925 --> 00:00:56.480
it's working.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.080
That's the meaning of three readings.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.520
Each time there is a different task.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:00.544
For the first time, 

00:01:00.544 --> 00:01:01.600
you just hold the big picture.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:02.640
Don't slow down.

00:01:02.641 --> 00:01:05.401
Don't highlight anything just so that the brain absorbs the shape of the idea.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.360
What is the main idea of the Ra SAO structure?

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.200
The second and third times are when you zoom in.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:11.760
Now you've captured the details.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.040
name the number of connections between ideas

00:01:14.041 --> 00:01:16.081
What you missed completely the first time.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:17.720
But here's what's important.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.680
even BA focused readings are still passive

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:21.681
Your brain is recognizing information, 

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:22.520
not pulling it out.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:24.120
and realizing is not remembering

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.960
Step two is where you fix that.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.760
Step 2 Preaching for the Wall

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.680
fold the book and put the notes away

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:30.720
Look at a wall.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.200
And explain what you've just read.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.640
out of memory

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:34.680
It doesn't have to be perfect.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.120
I can rephrase it in my own way.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:38.800
Your brain is now pulling information out.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:39.960
Instead of just recognizing it.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.160
And pulling Ra is what builds memory.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.840
Let's say you're studying.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:45.480
Read about how the immune system fights viruses.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.000
Now fold everything up.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:49.000
and explain it out loud as if preaching to a friend

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:50.600
You'll notice one thing right away.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.000
The parts you really understand will flow easily.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.455
The parts you don't understand, 

00:01:54.455 --> 00:01:55.240
you'll hit the wall.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.000
That wall is the most valuable thing.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.200
in your entire class.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.600
It shows you exactly where you need to go back and read.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:01.920
Let's do it a second time.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.440
That's the number 2 in the formula BA.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.240
2 second round of lectures

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.480
You'll fill in the gaps you missed in the first round.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.600
2 times pull out information actively completed

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.160
But there's a weakness.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.000
speak quickly

00:02:13.001 --> 00:02:15.161
You can go through the details and the mouth will fill in.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.200
empty with redundant words

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:17.200
Your brain is fooled.

00:02:17.201 --> 00:02:19.081
You think you know more than you do.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.720
That's why you need step three.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.720
step BA write as no AI look

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.440
Take a blank sheet of paper and write down everything you remember.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.240
no glancing no checking notes

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.200
Just let go of everything your brain can pull out.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:30.120
Writing slower than speaking

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:31.640
You can't lie on paper.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.600
All the gaps in your knowledge appear.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:35.240
into a white space looking straight at you.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.040
That's number one in BA two.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:38.920
Once written and it's a test.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.320
Be honest about what you really know.

00:02:41.321 --> 00:02:42.761
so what you write with the original

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.282
You'll see pink holes. 

00:02:44.282 --> 00:02:44.840
Fill them.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:47.320
Those pink holes are what your brain is about to forget.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.600
And now they're locked.
